NNAAMMEE
     sseemm__wwaaiitt, sseemm__ttrryywwaaiitt — decrement (lock) a semaphore

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Standard C Library (libc, -lc)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<sseemmaapphhoorree..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     sseemm__wwaaiitt(_s_e_m___t _*_s_e_m);

     _i_n_t
     sseemm__ttrryywwaaiitt(_s_e_m___t _*_s_e_m);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseemm__wwaaiitt() function decrements (locks) the semaphore pointed to by
     _s_e_m, but blocks if the value of _s_e_m is zero, until the value is non-zero
     and the value can be decremented.

     The sseemm__ttrryywwaaiitt() function decrements (locks) the semaphore pointed to by
     _s_e_m only if the value is non-zero.  Otherwise, the semaphore is not
     decremented and an error is returned.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Upon successful completion, the value 0 is returned; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The sseemm__wwaaiitt() and sseemm__ttrryywwaaiitt() functions will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The _s_e_m argument points to an invalid semaphore.

     Additionally, sseemm__wwaaiitt() will fail if:

     [EINTR]            A signal interrupted this function.

     Additionally, sseemm__ttrryywwaaiitt() will fail if:

     [EAGAIN]           The semaphore value was zero, and thus could not be
                        decremented.

